I have been developing an application based on the STEVAL-PTOOL1V1\_6S\_HL. I have managed to successfully get the motor up and running to the expected RPM using the speed potentiometer functionality.

I am now developing my own custom hardware using the STSPIN32F0B and I will not be using the speed potentiometer to control the speed of the motor. Instead my intention is to use the commands such as:

MC\_ProgramSpeedRampMotor1(2000, 1000);

MC\_StartMotor1();

To set the motor speed and start the motor.

I am unsure of how to go about removing the speed potentiometer functionality from the generated code In MC Workbench (V6.4.2) after loading in the STEVAL-PTOOL1V1\_6S\_HL.ioc the Potentiometer option visible can’t be changed
